 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Tensor-hom adjunction for module objects",
 "statement": "The derived hom of [def-sfb-derived-hom-modules] is right adjoint to the derived tensor\nproduct, as an adjunction with a parameter\n$-\\otimes^{\\mathrm L}_{\\Lambda_X}-\\dashv\\RHom_{\\Lambda_X}(-,-)$. In particular, for every\n$K\\in D(\\Mod_{\\Lambda_X})$ there is an adjunction\n$K\\otimes^{\\mathrm L}_{\\Lambda_X}-\\dashv\\RHom_{\\Lambda_X}(K,-)$, and\n$\\RHom_{\\Lambda_X}(K,-)$ is a right adjoint.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-proetale-coefficients/sk-def-sfb-derived-tensor-hom/def-sfb-derived-tensor-hom-adjunction-modules.md",
  "place": "node def-sfb-derived-tensor-hom-adjunction-modules, order 1624"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sfb-derived-hom-modules"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The internal hom of a closed monoidal category is right adjoint to the tensor product,\nnaturally in the parameter. Fixing the parameter $K$ gives the unary adjunction.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
